---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const raw=readFileSync('public/problem-framing/course-data.js','utf8');
const course=JSON.parse(raw.replace(/^window\.COURSE\s*=\s*/, '').replace(/;\s*$/, ''));
---
<Base title="How to Frame a Problem Well — A Course Hosted by Marcel Akiyama" description="A practical problem-framing course with foundations, worked examples, quizzes, exercises, and a final project. Examine evidence and compare competing explanations.">
 <header class="page-heading wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Field course / Product judgment</p><h1>How to frame<br/><em>a problem well.</em></h1><p class="page-lead">Learn to examine evidence, clarify goals, set boundaries, and compare explanations before committing to a solution.</p><div class="page-actions"><a class="solid-link" href="/problem-framing/">Open the interactive course →</a><a href="/problem-framing/reading/">Read the lessons as text</a></div></header>
 <div class="reading-layout wrap"><aside class="reading-aside"><span class="eyebrow">Learning resource</span><span>Foundations</span><span>10 practice modules</span><span>Final project</span></aside><article class="prose"><section><h2>Practice the judgment behind the methods.</h2><p>Start with an unclear brief. Separate what the team has observed from what it assumes. Develop competing frames, work out what evidence would distinguish them, and choose a useful next step.</p><p>The interactive version includes quizzes and exercises saved in your browser, with an option to export your workbook. The text edition makes the lessons available without JavaScript.</p></section><section><h2>What’s inside</h2><ol class="syllabus">{course.modules.map((m:{id:number,title:string,objective:string})=><li><a href={`/problem-framing/reading/#module-${m.id}`}>{m.title}</a><p>{m.objective}</p></li>)}</ol></section><section><h2>About this resource</h2><p>This course is hosted and maintained by Marcel Akiyama and was created with AI assistance. It is a learning resource, not an accredited qualification or a method guaranteed to prevent failure. The course includes research references and discusses the limits of its methods.</p><a class="arrow-link" href="/problem-framing/">Start exploring →</a></section></article></div>
</Base>
